13	procedimiento_respuesta_alarmas.pdf	2	1	1. Objetivo y niveles de severidad\nEste procedimiento indica como responder a las alarmas generadas por el sistema de telemetria.\nCada alarma tiene una de dos severidades, segun el umbral que supere el sensor:\nSeveridad\nCondicion\nTiempo maximo de respuesta\nOrden asociada\nAlerta\nEl valor supera el umbral de alerta del sensor\n24 horas\nCorrectiva de prioridad media\nCritica\nEl valor supera el umbral critico del sensor\n2 horas\nCorrectiva de prioridad alta\nEl tiempo de respuesta se cuenta desde el inicio de la alarma. Una alarma que sigue abierta al\ncambio de turno se informa explicitamente al turno entrante.	[-0.0038045,-0.0033126,-0.0158338,-0.0263032,0.0121074,0.003127,-0.0122285,-0.0106302,0.0168255,-0.0468334,-0.0490192,-0.0068728,-0.0049185,-0.0012072,0.0227241,0.0085979,0.0142016,-0.0010716,0.0239393,-0.033591,0.0227286,-0.0147376,0.0179366,-0.0152162,-0.0216882,0.0009604,0.0134911,-0.0184024,-0.0062464,0.2085897,-0.0356978,-0.0181488,-0.0128271,-0.0193138,0.0420358,-0.0351045,-0.0419634,-0.006523,0.0105679,-0.0168066,-0.0163819,0.0328298,-0.0121141,0.0301882,0.0009712,-0.0469685,-0.0561637,0.0376969,0.0104929,0.0120667,0.0051927,0.0055883,-0.0148839,0.050558,-0.0052229,0.0246027,0.0404364,0.0453908,0.0710358,0.036189,-0.0218475,0.0536308,0.0156584,-0.0016354,-0.0048134,0.0012033,0.0739476,-0.0002577,-0.0022077,0.0176924,0.0203742,0.0296022,-0.0095467,-0.0174156,0.0224324,-0.011106,-0.0609602,0.0509047,-0.062402,0.0111982,0.0434125,-0.0569178,-0.0321986,-0.0358391,-0.0151571,0.0455529,-0.0612015,-0.0248108,0.0290299,0.0258674,0.0168713,0.0242372,0.0107537,0.0105962,0.0003075,-0.0161204,0.0333316,0.0294981,-0.004074,0.0084229,-0.0133233,0.0269576,0.0046353,0.0018928,0.0090684,-0.002506,-0.0021834,0.0023552,0.0030806,0.0004568,-0.0180202,-0.2927125,0.0040726,0.0327902,-0.0022372,0.0876073,0.0191308,0.0169139,0.0416976,-0.0152358,0.0172095,0.0219539,-0.0281073,-0.0421712,-0.0012537,-0.0004724,0.0595672,-0.0061